  "limits": [
    "All 18 original-image proofs cover three diagnostic candidates on one retained biquadratic network fixture, not arbitrary NetworkSrf inputs. The previously inconclusive arc-length source index 1 certifies within the unchanged 1e-6 absolute tolerance and two-million-operation exact budget.",
    "Degree, arithmetic, depth and interval-work limits are unchanged. Exact original-tensor restrictions supply certificate geometry; numerical isocurve searches only propose UV curves. The assembled returned UV curve is independently certified.",
    "The cache retains one fixed-coordinate restriction, bounded by original variable-direction controls and spans. Supported tensors have no full-order internal discontinuities; incident patches therefore agree at shared knots.",
    "Certificates prove directed continuous source-curve-to-surface correspondence, not injectivity, topology, symmetric distance or surface continuity. Curve refitting retains its separate adaptive sampled source-fit policy.",
    "Surface tensors and saved Rhino returned-point comparisons are unchanged. All three comparisons remain above 1e-6; NetworkSrf remains unregistered. Interior fitting policy, broader comparisons and runtime/performance qualification remain unfinished.",
    "SMLib, SM_API and adapter archives are instrumented by AddressSanitizer. Rust and separately bundled dependencies are not separately instrumented; leak and optional stack-use-after-return checks are disabled."
